        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "So let's get started writing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 5.85,
          "en": "our first custom React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 8.88,
          "en": "by building our first custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.88,
          "end": 11.13,
          "en": "As mentioned, components are these functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.13,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "that return JSX code and as a React developer you'll write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "dozens, and hundreds, and thousands of those components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 21.75,
          "en": "to build up your React applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.75,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "Now we're about to build a Twitter-like demo application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 28.02,
          "en": "where random people can post their stuff",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.02,
          "end": 30.93,
          "en": "for the entire world to read it, amazing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.93,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "And along the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 35.43,
          "en": "whilst building that application, that demo website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.43,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "we'll dive into many core React features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "And we'll get started now by building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "our first custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "Now for this demo application which we're about to build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "there are actually multiple possible components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "we could identify.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 53.7,
          "en": "We could, for example, build this button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.7,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "as a separate component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 59.22,
          "en": "Or this list of posts of tweets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.22,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "if you wanna call it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 62.64,
          "en": "Or the individual tweets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "And indeed, that is how you should think of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "and React applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "We have all these building blocks, and we then build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 72.813,
          "en": "the overall UI by combining them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.92,
          "end": 76.89,
          "en": "Now, of course, you don't have to put every single character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.89,
          "end": 78.27,
          "en": "into its own component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.27,
          "end": 82.53,
          "en": "but it makes sense to group related functionalities together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "into different building blocks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 86.16,
          "en": "And here we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.16,
          "end": 90.15,
          "en": "start by taking a closer look at the individual posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 92.19,
          "en": "And the first custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.19,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "which I wanna build together with you, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 98.31,
          "en": "is a component for such a single post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.31,
          "end": 101.28,
          "en": "And later, we'll be able to then output multiple posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 101.28,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "based on that custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "Now therefore, back in this project, which I gave you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "I'll go to that source folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 112.803,
          "en": "and in there add a new folder called components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "Now this name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "You don't have to name this folder, components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 121.86,
          "en": "You don't even have to create a folder in the first place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 126.39,
          "en": "but it makes sense to group your component files together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "into such a folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "Now this app JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 132.63,
          "en": "which technically also contains that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 132.63,
          "end": 136.53,
          "en": "is not part of that folder because that will soon be our",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.53,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "And I'll get back to the concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 141.453,
          "en": "of our root component later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "So for the moment, let's go to components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 148.95,
          "en": "And in there I'll add a new file called post.jsx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 148.95,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "The name is of course up to you, but post makes sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "since we're about to add the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "that defines a single post in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.26,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "The markup that defines a single post, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "and the .jsx is required because we plan on writing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "of JSX code in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 170.49,
          "en": "If we had just .js that would work in projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.49,
          "end": 173.07,
          "en": "created with create React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.07,
          "end": 178.07,
          "en": "but Vite projects actually want .jsx to support JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 179.19,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "in JavaScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "And now as a next step, we have to create a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 189.03,
          "en": "Because React components are just functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 189.03,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "It's as simple as that regular JavaScript functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 194.97,
          "en": "with one special gotcha though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 194.97,
          "end": 197.4,
          "en": "the name of your functions should start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 199.443,
          "en": "with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "And, of course, the name also should describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 205.23,
          "en": "what this component will be about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 205.23,
          "end": 209.07,
          "en": "So here I plan on defining the markup that defines",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 209.07,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "an individual post in that grid of posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 215.61,
          "en": "And therefore, I'll name the function post like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 215.61,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "And the upper-case starting character is important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "it's not required technically in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 226.14,
          "en": "but it is a recommendation, and it will be required later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 229.89,
          "en": "Now, this function should be exported so that it can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.89,
          "end": 232.65,
          "en": "in our code files as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 232.65,
          "end": 235.89,
          "en": "And for that, you can use the standard modern JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.89,
          "end": 239.67000000000002,
          "en": "export syntax, where you either export it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 242.61,
          "en": "by adding the export keyword in front of the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.61,
          "end": 244.8,
          "en": "or as a file default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.8,
          "end": 249.27,
          "en": "And the only difference is then regarding how you import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 249.27,
          "end": 251.343,
          "en": "that function in another file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.39,
          "end": 254.43,
          "en": "So here I export it as a default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.43,
          "end": 257.7,
          "en": "And now in that function, as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.7,
          "end": 260.34,
          "en": "we should return some JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.34,
          "end": 263.76,
          "en": "because that is what turns a regular function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 263.76,
          "end": 265.98,
          "en": "into a React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "It's really only the fact that you start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 272.19,
          "en": "with an upper-case character and even more important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 272.19,
          "end": 274.353,
          "en": "that you return some JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 275.34000000000003,
          "end": 278.43,
          "en": "Now for a single post to get started here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 278.43,
          "end": 280.5,
          "en": "we could return a div,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 280.5,
          "end": 282.9,
          "en": "and then in there may be a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.9,
          "end": 286.53,
          "en": "where we output the name of the author of the post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 286.53,
          "end": 291.42,
          "en": "And below that another paragraph with the post body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 291.42,
          "end": 293.553,
          "en": "like React.js is awesome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 295.53,
          "end": 298.95,
          "en": "Now, after hitting my auto format shortcut here in VS code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 298.95,
          "end": 302.49,
          "en": "I get this function and that is now indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 302.49,
          "end": 305.733,
          "en": "our first custom React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 307.35,
          "end": 310.32,
          "en": "But, of course, if we just add this file like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 310.32,
          "end": 314.88,
          "en": "and save all changes, nothing changes on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.88,
          "end": 315.75,
          "en": "And by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 315.75,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "you must make sure to keep that NPM run dev process here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 322.05,
          "en": "up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322.05,
          "end": 324.677,
          "en": "In case of a create React app project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 324.677,
          "end": 328.89,
          "en": "it was NPM start with vite its NPM run dev,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 328.89,
          "end": 331.32,
          "en": "and this starts a development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 331.32,
          "end": 333.6,
          "en": "which watches your code files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 333.6,
          "end": 336.48,
          "en": "serves your website on the address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 336.48,
          "end": 339,
          "en": "that's being output here in the terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 343.38,
          "en": "in my case, local host 5173 so that you can preview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 343.38,
          "end": 346.473,
          "en": "your React website there as you are building it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 347.4,
          "end": 350.19,
          "en": "And it will automatically reload the website here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 350.19,
          "end": 353.88,
          "en": "and update the website and update what you see on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 353.88,
          "end": 357.48,
          "en": "as you make and save changes to your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 357.48,
          "end": 360.753,
          "en": "So that's why this process must keep up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 361.98,
          "end": 365.52,
          "en": "But with that, we still don't see our post content here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.52,
          "end": 367.74,
          "en": "We still see, Hello World.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.74,
          "end": 371.1,
          "en": "The reason for that is that I created this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 371.1,
          "end": 373.98,
          "en": "this post component in a separate file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 373.98,
          "end": 375.69,
          "en": "but I'm not using it anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 375.69,
          "end": 379.53,
          "en": "It's the same as with a regular JavaScript function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 379.53,
          "end": 384.53,
          "en": "If I add a function called, add, where I do something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 384.9,
          "end": 387.03,
          "en": "even if I export that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 387.03,
          "end": 389.223,
          "en": "it's still not getting used anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 390.09,
          "end": 393.03,
          "en": "Instead, exporting is just the first step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 393.03,
          "end": 395.73,
          "en": "to make it usable outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 395.73,
          "end": 399,
          "en": "But we then have to use the function outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 399,
          "end": 401.553,
          "en": "And it's the same with this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 402.78,
          "end": 406.40999999999997,
          "en": "Now the place where we want to use our component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 406.40999999999997,
          "end": 410.19,
          "en": "is inside of JSX code of other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 410.19,
          "end": 413.1,
          "en": "So you build your complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 413.1,
          "end": 415.35,
          "en": "by combining components with each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 415.35,
          "end": 418.44,
          "en": "and nesting components into each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 418.44,
          "end": 421.05,
          "en": "Now at the moment we have two places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 421.05,
          "end": 424.71,
          "en": "where we do have some JSX code in use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 424.71,
          "end": 428.79,
          "en": "That's the main JSX file where we pass some JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 428.79,
          "end": 433.323,
          "en": "to render and app JSX where I return, Hello World.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 434.46,
          "end": 438.63,
          "en": "Now in both places we could output our post component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 438.63,
          "end": 442.32,
          "en": "but typically, when building React user interfaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 442.32,
          "end": 444.57,
          "en": "you have one root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 444.57,
          "end": 448.77,
          "en": "So one single component that's being output in main JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 448.77,
          "end": 452.4,
          "en": "and in this case, that would be the app component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 452.4,
          "end": 454.89,
          "en": "And then inside of that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 454.89,
          "end": 457.5,
          "en": "inside of the app component in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 457.5,
          "end": 460.44,
          "en": "and any components used by that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 460.44,
          "end": 463.44,
          "en": "you use your other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 463.44,
          "end": 466.2,
          "en": "So the post component should be used in the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 466.2,
          "end": 468.24,
          "en": "of the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 468.24,
          "end": 471,
          "en": "So there, instead of outputting Hello World,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 471,
          "end": 473.943,
          "en": "we could output post like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 474.93,
          "end": 476.19,
          "en": "Now in order to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 476.19,
          "end": 479.4,
          "en": "we have to import that component function though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 479.4,
          "end": 482.22,
          "en": "and we do that by using the import keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 482.22,
          "end": 487.22,
          "en": "and then post from ./components/Post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 487.23,
          "end": 490.92,
          "en": "And the file extension should be omitted, as mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 490.92,
          "end": 495.69,
          "en": "But you have to specify the full relative path from app JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 495.69,
          "end": 498.123,
          "en": "to that post .jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 499.35,
          "end": 503.25,
          "en": "So with that, we're importing this post component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 503.25,
          "end": 504.96,
          "en": "and even though it's a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 504.96,
          "end": 508.02,
          "en": "we're not using it like you would normally use functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 508.02,
          "end": 509.49,
          "en": "by executing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 509.49,
          "end": 513.6,
          "en": "but instead, we're using it like an HTML element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 513.6,
          "end": 516.57,
          "en": "in this JSX code that's returned by app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 516.57,
          "end": 519.213,
          "en": "In this case, it's the only element that's returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 520.11,
          "end": 523.56,
          "en": "And that's the special thing about your component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 523.56,
          "end": 527.16,
          "en": "They are standard JavaScript functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 527.16,
          "end": 530.25,
          "en": "but you can use them in JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 530.25,
          "end": 533.52,
          "en": "and behind the scenes React will basically execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 533.52,
          "end": 536.01,
          "en": "your component functions for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 536.01,
          "end": 540.54,
          "en": "Take a look at the html Vite JSX code to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 540.54,
          "end": 542.16,
          "en": "that's returned by them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 542.16,
          "end": 546.48,
          "en": "And then build the overall user interface and render it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 546.48,
          "end": 547.53,
          "en": "to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 547.53,
          "end": 550.38,
          "en": "That's what React is doing for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 550.38,
          "end": 553.32,
          "en": "So React is then generating the browser instructions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 553.32,
          "end": 556.65,
          "en": "that are needed to bring your HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 556.65,
          "end": 558.633,
          "en": "to life in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 559.89,
          "end": 562.02,
          "en": "Now what's really important is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 562.02,
          "end": 567.02,
          "en": "in the place where you use a component function in JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 567.48,
          "end": 571.95,
          "en": "like we're doing it here with post or in main JSX with app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 571.95,
          "end": 574.41,
          "en": "your component functions must start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 574.41,
          "end": 576.87,
          "en": "with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 576.87,
          "end": 580.86,
          "en": "It's optional in the file where you define them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 580.86,
          "end": 583.62,
          "en": "but there you typically also start their names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 583.62,
          "end": 585.84,
          "en": "with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 585.84,
          "end": 588.6,
          "en": "But it's absolutely required in the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 588.6,
          "end": 591.39,
          "en": "where you use your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 591.39,
          "end": 596.39,
          "en": "So in app JSX where I import post from the post JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 596.52,
          "end": 600.93,
          "en": "this name here post must start with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 600.93,
          "end": 603.9,
          "en": "It should not start with a lowercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 603.9,
          "end": 607.71,
          "en": "because in the JSX code you add to your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 607.71,
          "end": 610.59,
          "en": "elements that start with a lowercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 610.59,
          "end": 613.05,
          "en": "are considered to be default elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 613.05,
          "end": 616.62,
          "en": "So React will try to find a default HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 616.62,
          "end": 617.76,
          "en": "with that name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 617.76,
          "end": 620.433,
          "en": "which it would not find in case of post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 621.27,
          "end": 624.33,
          "en": "And elements starting with the uppercase character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 624.33,
          "end": 627.21,
          "en": "are considered to be custom components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 627.21,
          "end": 629.97,
          "en": "And in that case, React will go ahead and execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 629.97,
          "end": 632.823,
          "en": "your custom component function as mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 633.81,
          "end": 635.76,
          "en": "But that's why default elements like div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 635.76,
          "end": 638.52,
          "en": "are written like this and do not start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 638.52,
          "end": 640.47,
          "en": "with an upper-case character,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 640.47,
          "end": 643.2,
          "en": "but your own components must start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 643.2,
          "end": 646.59,
          "en": "with an upper-case character when using them in JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 646.59,
          "end": 650.25,
          "en": "And that's really an important rule to memorize.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 650.25,
          "end": 652.26,
          "en": "But with all of that out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 652.26,
          "end": 656.55,
          "en": "if we save everything, we get this content on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 656.55,
          "end": 659.07,
          "en": "And this is now the content we defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 659.07,
          "end": 661.77,
          "en": "in our own post component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 661.77,
          "end": 663.99,
          "en": "So even though it's not super fancy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 663.99,
          "end": 666.87,
          "en": "and definitely not interactive in any way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 666.87,
          "end": 670.71,
          "en": "it is our first custom component defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 670.71,
          "end": 673.443,
          "en": "and used in our React project.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
